---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Website Terms of Use | Brighter Sites"
  description="Review the general terms that apply when using the Brighter Sites marketing website and public demo experiences."
>
  <section class="page-intro legal-intro">
    <div class="container legal-shell">
      <p class="eyebrow">Website terms</p>
      <h1>Terms of Use</h1>
      <p class="page-lead">
        These terms apply to use of the Brighter Sites marketing website and
        public demonstration websites. Client projects and paid services are
        governed by separate project agreements.
      </p>
      <div class="legal-review-note" role="note">
        <strong>Draft for attorney review.</strong>
        <span>This version is being prepared for launch and is not yet the effective production terms.</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section legal-section">
    <div class="container legal-shell legal-copy">
      <section>
        <h2>1. General website use</h2>
        <p>
          Brighter Sites provides this website to explain its website design,
          development, launch, and optional ongoing-management services. You may
          browse and use the site for lawful informational and business purposes.
          By using the site, you agree not to interfere with its operation,
          attempt unauthorized access, misuse security features, or use the site
          in a way that violates applicable law or another person’s rights.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>2. No client relationship from browsing</h2>
        <p>
          Visiting this website, viewing a demo, or sending an initial inquiry
          does not by itself create a client relationship or obligate Brighter
          Sites to accept a project. A website project or paid service begins only
          under the applicable proposal, statement of work, service agreement,
          accepted change order, or other project document.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>3. Separate client agreements control paid services</h2>
        <p>
          These public Website Terms of Use do not replace the Website Services
          Agreement, Website Ownership and Service Exit Terms, Proposal/SOW,
          service-plan terms, or other project-specific documents accepted by a
          Brighter Sites client. If a client agreement addresses a paid service,
          project, ownership right, handoff obligation, fee, warranty, or remedy,
          the applicable client agreement controls that matter.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>4. Demonstration websites</h2>
        <p>
          Brighter Sites may publish demonstration websites to show different
          design directions, page structures, content depth, and user experiences.
          Unless a demo clearly identifies a real customer, names, practices,
          clinicians, locations, testimonials, scheduling details, and other demo
          content should be understood as demonstration material rather than a
          representation that the featured provider or practice exists or offers
          services.
        </p>
        <p>
          Demo websites are examples of design and development capability, not a
          promise that every client project will use the same structure, features,
          page count, imagery, copy, performance, search visibility, or business
          results.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>5. Informational content and no professional advice</h2>
        <p>
          Content on the Brighter Sites website is general business and website
          information. It is not legal, tax, accounting, medical, mental-health,
          regulatory, accessibility-certification, or other professional advice.
          Brighter Sites does not determine whether a visitor or client satisfies
          every law, professional rule, privacy requirement, accessibility
          requirement, advertising rule, or industry-specific obligation.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>6. No guaranteed search or business results</h2>
        <p>
          Brighter Sites may describe practices intended to support usability,
          performance, search visibility, measurement, and conversion. Search
          engines, directories, browsers, networks, third-party services, market
          conditions, and visitor behavior are outside Brighter Sites’ control.
          The website does not promise a particular search ranking, indexing time,
          traffic level, lead volume, conversion rate, appointment volume,
          revenue, or other business outcome.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>7. Intellectual property</h2>
        <p>
          Unless otherwise indicated, the Brighter Sites name, branding, website
          design, public website copy, graphics, code, and other original material
          on this site are owned by or licensed to Brighter Sites and are protected
          by applicable intellectual-property laws. You may view and reasonably
          share links to public pages, but you may not copy or republish a
          substantial portion of the site, remove ownership notices, impersonate
          Brighter Sites, or commercially redistribute Brighter Sites material
          without permission or another lawful basis.
        </p>
        <p>
          Customer names, logos, trademarks, licensed media, open-source software,
          and third-party materials remain subject to their respective owners’
          rights and licenses.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>8. External links and third-party services</h2>
        <p>
          This website may link to the Brighter Sites client portal, demonstration
          websites, scheduling or communication tools, and unrelated third-party
          services. Brighter Sites does not control unrelated third-party sites
          and is not responsible for their content, availability, security,
          pricing, terms, or privacy practices. A link does not necessarily mean
          Brighter Sites endorses every statement or service on the destination.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>9. Contact and sensitive information</h2>
        <p>
          The public contact path is intended for ordinary business inquiries. Do
          not send passwords, recovery codes, payment-card information, Social
          Security numbers, protected health information (PHI), medical details,
          or other highly sensitive or regulated information through ordinary
          email or other Brighter Sites systems unless Brighter Sites has
          expressly accepted that information under a compliant project scope.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>10. Availability and accuracy</h2>
        <p>
          Brighter Sites uses reasonable care in maintaining the website but does
          not guarantee that every page will always be available, current,
          complete, compatible with every device, or free from errors. Pricing,
          offers, service descriptions, examples, third-party costs, and other
          information may change. A project-specific written agreement controls
          over general marketing content when the two differ.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>11. Privacy</h2>
        <p>
          Information handled through the website, client portal, and related
          workflows is addressed in the <a href="/privacy/">Brighter Sites Privacy Policy</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>12. Changes to these terms</h2>
        <p>
          Brighter Sites may update these Terms of Use as the website, services,
          or legal requirements change. The current version will be posted on
          this page with an effective or revision date when approved for
          production use. Changes to these public terms do not silently amend an
          already accepted client project agreement.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>13. Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Questions about these website terms may be sent to
          <a href="mailto:help@brightersites.app">help@brightersites.app</a>.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .legal-shell {
    max-width: 54rem;
  }

  .legal-intro h1 {
    max-width: 13ch;
  }

  .legal-review-note {
    display: grid;
    gap: .3rem;
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
    padding: 1rem 1.1rem;
    border-left: 3px solid var(--teal);
    background: var(--teal-light);
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }

  .legal-review-note strong {
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .legal-section {
    padding-top: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 4rem);
  }

  .legal-copy {
    display: grid;
    gap: 2.2rem;
  }

  .legal-copy section {
    padding-bottom: 2rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .legal-copy section:last-child {
    padding-bottom: 0;
    border-bottom: 0;
  }

  .legal-copy h2 {
    margin-bottom: .8rem;
    color: var(--ink);
    font-size: clamp(1.35rem, 2.6vw, 1.8rem);
  }

  .legal-copy p,
  .legal-copy li {
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    line-height: 1.75;
  }

  .legal-copy p + p,
  .legal-copy p + ul,
  .legal-copy ul + p {
    margin-top: .85rem;
  }

  .legal-copy ul {
    display: grid;
    gap: .55rem;
    margin: .85rem 0 0 1.25rem;
  }

  .legal-copy a {
    color: var(--teal-dark);
    font-weight: 750;
  }
</style>
